{
  "abstract": "For the ideal two-step Boschi–Hardy ladder with three binary settings per observer and five exact zeros, the fixed-state maximum for four positive Schmidt coefficients is the best of three disjoint pairings. The proof covers arbitrary complex binary effects and gives attaining projective measurements. Equality at the two-qubit plastic-constant value holds exactly when both pairs have smaller-to-larger ratio ρ⁻². A finite mixture of pure components through Schmidt rank four obeys the same ceiling. Every full-rank pure qutrit is strictly below it. A pure state with twelve distinct positive Schmidt weights attains the value through six orthogonal qubit sectors.",
